unity-gtk4-menu (0.7) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Give stand-ins for class actions the enabled state of the action they
    stand for, and follow it. GTK has no getter for it, only
    gtk_widget_action_set_enabled(), so that is intercepted - through the
    PLT for C and Rust applications, through g_module_symbol() for gjs and
    Python - every call remembered on the widget, and applied to the
    stand-in when it is created and whenever it changes. Items that were
    always shown enabled now grey out when the application disables them,
    and items the application hides when disabled (hidden-when) are hidden
    in the global menu too: gnome-text-editor no longer lists both
    "Fullscreen" and "Leave Fullscreen", and loupe greys out Print and
    Delete until an image is open.
  * tests/classtest.c: a class action disabled in init and one that can be
    toggled over D-Bus. tests/gjstest.js: the same for gjs.

 -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:30:00 +0000

unity-gtk4-menu (0.6) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Reach gjs and PyGObject applications. They do not link GTK4; GObject
    Introspection loads it after our constructor has run, so the library
    found no GTK4 and did nothing - gnome-characters, gnome-weather,
    gnome-tweaks, showtime and gnome-music had no global menu. Intercept
    g_module_symbol(), through which introspection resolves every function
    before calling it, and hook GTK4 at the first gtk_ or adw_ lookup, when
    it is mapped but none of its classes is initialised yet. The lookup is
    handed on unchanged, and the hook runs after it: gtk-nocsd, also
    preloaded in Ubuntu Unity, intercepts the same function and only fetches
    its GTK types there - hooking first made it miss them, and
    gnome-characters aborted.

 -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 00:10:00 +0000

unity-gtk4-menu (0.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Export the window's main menu rather than the first menu button found.
    Five of thirteen applications measured have a secondary menu earlier in
    the widget tree - gnome-calculator's mode selector, gnome-logs's boot
    list, simple-scan's scan type, gnome-text-editor's search options and
    nautilus's folder menu - and got that one in the global menu instead.
    Candidates are now ranked by: shown (visible, and not under a container
    that keeps it hidden), marked primary with gtk_menu_button_set_primary(),
    number of app. and win. items, then tree order.

 -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:45:00 +0000

unity-gtk4-menu (0.4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Make menu items that name widget class actions work in the global menu.
    An action installed with gtk_widget_class_install_action() is resolved
    through the widget's action muxer inside the application, but is not in
    the window's exported action group, so Unity showed the item greyed out -
    yelp's "About Help" (win.yelp-show-about-dialog) is one. The exported
    copy of the model now points such items at a stand-in in the window's
    action map, which activates the original name from the menu's owner
    widget. Property actions and names with a prefix other than app. or win.
    are left as they are.
  * Handle each GtkApplicationWindow once per realize rather than twice: its
    realize chains up to GtkWindow's, which is hooked too.

 -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 23:10:00 +0000

unity-gtk4-menu (0.3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Drop menu items that carry a "custom" attribute before exporting, along
    with any section left empty by the removal. They are slots for live
    widgets inside a GtkPopoverMenu, which cannot cross D-Bus, and arrived in
    the global menu as blank rows - yelp's zoom controls did exactly that.

 -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 11:30:00 +0000

unity-gtk4-menu (0.2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Resolve every GTK and GLib symbol with dlsym at runtime instead of linking
    them. Version 0.1 had libgtk-4.so.1 in NEEDED, and since the library is
    preloaded into every process on the machine it dragged GTK4 into GTK3
    processes and killed unity-settings-daemon, onboard, apport-gtk and the
    indicators.
  * Do nothing at all unless GTK4 is already loaded in the process, tested with
    dlopen(RTLD_NOLOAD).
  * Build target "check" fails if a GTK or GLib library reappears in NEEDED.

 -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:45:00 +0000

unity-gtk4-menu (0.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Exports a GTK4 header bar menu to the Unity global menu
    and the HUD by setting it as the application menu bar before realize.
  * show-application-name setting controls whether the exported entry is named
    after the application or given a neutral label.

